{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Inputs of the heavy Docs Checks suites. A same-repository pull request skips a suite only when no file matched by shared_inputs or by the suite's inputs differs between the trusted base checkout and the pull-request head. Main pushes, the nightly run, manual dispatches and fork pull requests run every suite. Patterns are repository-relative POSIX paths: a plain path names one file, a trailing /** names a directory tree, and *, ? and [] are shell-style wildcards that may also match a slash. The lists were derived by tracing every file each suite opens, lists or globs while it runs (Python audit hooks, child processes included), then widened to whole directories where a suite enumerates them.",
